Day-22
---------

Locators
---------
1.We can identify various elements on the web using Locators.
2.Locators are address that identify a web element uniquely within the page.


 types of Locators:
1)Locators
*id
*name
*Linktext or partialLinkText
*Class Name  -->used for group of web elements.
*TagName    -->used for group of web elements.
these are used to identify specific web elements.


findElement() --->single webelement
findElements() --->multiple webelements

Scenario 1: Locator matching with single web element
findElement(loc) --->single web element   WebElement
findElements(loc) --->single web element   List<WebElement>


Scenario 2: Locator matching with multi web element
findElement(loc) --->single web element   WebElement
findElements(loc) --->single web element   List<WebElement>

Scenario 3: Locator is not matching with any element
findElement(loc) ---> No suchelement Exception
findElements(loc) ---> it will not throw any exception.returns 0


2)Customized locators
*CSS Selector
->Tag and id
->Tag and Class
->Tag and attribute
->Tag class and attribute

*XPath
->Absolute XPath
->Relative XPath
